# User Features (`app/user.py`)

## Saved Filter Profiles (`/user/profiles`)

Allows users to save and restore named dashboard filter configurations.

### API
| Route | Method | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `/user/profiles` | GET | Page render |
| `/user/profiles/list?show_all=0` | GET | JSON list, ordered `is_starred DESC, name ASC`. Returns user's own + any `is_shared` profile; super admin can pass `show_all=1` |
| `/user/profiles/save` | POST JSON | `{name, filter_data}` — filter_data is the full dashboard filter state dict |
| `/user/profiles/<id>/data` | GET | Returns `{id, name, filter_data}` for restoring on dashboard. Owner / super admin / any logged-in user if `is_shared=True` |
| `/user/profiles/<id>` | DELETE | Owner or super admin only |
| `/user/profiles/bulk-delete` | POST JSON | `{ids: []}` |
| `/user/profiles/<id>/star` | POST JSON | `{is_starred: bool}` — toggle if omitted (owner / super admin) |
| `/user/profiles/<id>/share` | POST JSON | `{is_shared: bool}` — toggle if omitted (**super admin only**) |

### filter_data JSON structure
Same keys as the dashboard filter form: `subject`, `source_type`, `years`, `topics`, `subtopics`, `chapters`, `levels`, `q_type`, `qid_search`, `sort_config`, etc.

The dashboard JS serialises the current form state into this blob when saving, and restores it by re-populating the filter form when loading.

### Dashboard "Load profile" dropdown
A small `bi-folder2-open` icon button sits next to the save (`bi-floppy`) button in the Filters card header. Clicking it opens a Bootstrap `dropdown-menu` (`#filterProfileMenu`) built by `loadFilterProfilesDropdown()` on `DOMContentLoaded`. The menu is structured as section headers (`<h6 class="dropdown-header">`) + dividers: **Starred**, **My profiles**, **Shared by admins**, plus a fixed "Manage profiles" footer link. Each item carries `data-profile-id` and on click calls `onFilterProfileSelect(id)` → fetches `/user/profiles/<id>/data` → `convertProfileToSettings()` → `restoreFilterSettings()` → `htmx.trigger(filterForm, 'submit')`. The menu is refreshed after a successful save.

## Saved Generation Presets (`/user/gen-profiles`)

Reusable generation-option templates. **Options only** — never store `question_ids` or `filter_data`.

Backed by `SavedGenerationProfile` (user_id, name, options_data JSON, is_starred, is_shared, created_at, updated_at).

### API
| Route | Method | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `/user/gen-profiles` | GET | Page render (`saved_gen_profiles.html`) |
| `/user/gen-profiles/list?show_all=0` | GET | JSON list, ordered `is_starred DESC, name ASC`. Returns user's own + any `is_shared` preset |
| `/user/gen-profiles/save` | POST JSON | `{name, options_data}` — upsert by `(user_id, name)`; `question_ids` is stripped server-side |
| `/user/gen-profiles/<id>/data` | GET | `{id, name, is_starred, options_data}` — accessible to owner / super admin / any logged-in user if shared |
| `/user/gen-profiles/<id>` | DELETE | Owner or super admin only |
| `/user/gen-profiles/bulk-delete` | POST JSON | `{ids: []}` |
| `/user/gen-profiles/<id>/star` | POST JSON | `{is_starred: bool}` — toggle if omitted |
| `/user/gen-profiles/<id>/share` | POST JSON | `{is_shared: bool}` — toggle if omitted (**super admin only**) |

### options_data JSON structure
Same shape as `GeneratedFile.generation_options` (see [document-generation.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/document-generation.mdc)) minus `question_ids`.

The Generate-page JS (`getCurrentGenerationOptions()` in `templates/generate.html`) builds this dict by reading every option control, and `restoreGenerationOptions()` applies it back. Loading a preset never touches the hidden `question_ids`, `sort_config`, or `filter_data` form inputs bound to the current selection.

### Starring
Both `SavedFilter` and `SavedGenerationProfile` have an `is_starred` boolean column (indexed). List endpoints return starred items first; the Generate-page and Dashboard dropdowns group them under a `★ Starred` optgroup.

### Sharing
Both tables also have an `is_shared` boolean column (indexed). Only **super admins** can toggle `is_shared` (via `/share` endpoints). Shared profiles/presets appear in every user's list and dropdowns:
- List pages show a green `Shared` badge plus the owner's username; non-owners cannot delete or star them.
- The dashboard and generate dropdowns group shared rows under a `Shared by admins` optgroup with the owner's name appended.
- `/data` endpoints accept any logged-in user when `is_shared=True` so shared profiles can be applied by anyone.

## Saved Question Sets (`/user/sets`)

Subject-scoped named collections of question IDs. **See [question-sets.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/question-sets.mdc)** for the full reference (model, API, dashboard set-algebra modal, URL apply flow).

Quick recap: `SavedQuestionSet (user_id, name, subject FK, question_ids JSON, is_starred, is_shared, created_at, updated_at)`, upsert by `(user, subject, name)`, parallel `is_shared` super-admin-only mechanism, dashboard chip-builder modal triggered by the **Set** button between Manage and Generate.

## My Generated Files (`/user/files`)

Section-organised view of every `GeneratedFile`. Each user owns one default ("Latest") section plus any custom sections they create; files drag-and-drop across sections; super-admin can share files or whole sections with selected users.

### Models in play
- `FileSection (user_id, name UNIQUE per user, sort_order, sort_field, sort_direction, page_size, collapsed, is_default, created_at, updated_at)` — sort_field ∈ `{name, created_at, completed_at, question_count, manual}`; sort_direction ∈ `{asc, desc}`; page_size ∈ `{5, 10, 25, 50, 100}`.
- `FileShare (file_id?, section_id?, shared_by_user_id, shared_with_user_id)` — XOR check on (file_id, section_id). Exactly one row per (target, file) or (target, section) thanks to unique constraints. ON DELETE CASCADE from both parents.
- `GeneratedFile.section_id` (FK to `file_sections`, ON DELETE SET NULL) + `manual_position` (int, used only when section.sort_field == 'manual').
- Default-section invariant: `_get_or_create_default_section(user_id)` in `app/user.py` lazy-creates the `is_default=True` row on first /user/files load AND whenever the generator records a new file. The helper is race-safe (rolls back + re-queries on IntegrityError). New files always land in this section; deletion of any other section moves its files back to default.

### API (page + sections)
| Route | Method | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `/user/files` | GET | Page render (renders `my_files.html`); auto-creates the default section |
| `/user/sections?show_all=` | GET | List user's own sections + virtual `id=-1` "Shared with me" entry (only when at least one share exists). Each row carries `file_count`, sort + page state, `is_default`, `is_shared_in`, `owner_username`. Super-admin with `show_all=1` returns **every** user's sections (own first, then ordered by `user_id`); `owner_username` is populated on foreign rows so the client can render a header pill. The virtual "Shared with me" row is omitted in `show_all` mode (the admin already sees the source files directly) |
| `/user/sections` | POST | `{name}` — create. 409 on name collision |
| `/user/sections/<id>` | PATCH | Partial: `{name?, sort_field?, sort_direction?, page_size?, collapsed?}`. Default section cannot be renamed but its sort + page_size + collapsed are tweakable |
| `/user/sections/<id>` | DELETE | Owner or super admin. Default section cannot be deleted. Contained files auto-move to default |
| `/user/sections/reorder` | POST | `{ids:[...]}` — `sort_order = index + 1`. Default is always pinned to 0 |

### API (files)
| Route | Method | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `/user/files/list?section_id=&page=&show_all=&q=` | GET | Paginated single-section listing. `section_id=-1` returns shared-with-me. `show_all=1` for super admin includes other owners. Optional `q` is a case-insensitive substring filter against `display_name` and `filename` (applied before sort+paginate) used by the page-level search box so matches span every page of the section. Response: `{section_id, page, page_size, total, pages, files:[...]}` |
| `/user/files/<id>/filter` | GET | Get saved filter_data for "Re-filter" button |
| `/user/files/<id>/generation_options` | GET | Get saved generation_options + display_name for re-generate |
| `/generate/pdf/<id>` | GET | **Lazy PDF.** Builds and/or serves the PDF (or PDF-zip) sibling next to the row's docx/zip. First call runs Word COM synchronously; subsequent calls send the cached file. JSON errors on 403/404/409/503/500 for fetch-driven frontend |
| `/user/files/<id>/move` | POST | `{section_id}` — owner or super admin; target must be a section owned by the file's owner |
| `/user/files/bulk-move` | POST | `{ids:[], section_id}` — same constraints; non-owned IDs are silently skipped |
| `/user/files/<id>/rename` | POST | `{display_name}` — renames the DB row only; filename on disk stays unchanged |
| `/user/files/reorder` | POST | `{section_id, ids:[]}` — sets each file's `manual_position` to its index, and switches `section.sort_field` to `manual` so the new order is what users see |
| `/user/files/<id>` | DELETE | Deletes DB record + file on disk |
| `/user/files/bulk-delete` | POST JSON | `{ids: []}` |
| `/user/files/bulk-download` | POST JSON | `{ids: []}` → streams `application/zip` named `my-files-<ts>.zip`. Skips non-completed and missing-on-disk; dedupes display names via `(2)`, `(3)`, ... suffix |

### API (sharing — super admin only)
| Route | Method | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `/user/shares?file_id=` or `?section_id=` | GET | `{shares: [{id, user_id, username, created_at}], available_users: [...]}` |
| `/user/shares` | POST | `{file_id?\|section_id?, user_ids:[]}` — upserts. Adds missing rows, deletes ones not in `user_ids`. Owner cannot be a target |
| `/user/shares/<id>` | DELETE | Revoke one row |
| `/user/shares/users` | GET | All users, for the picker |

The default section is not shareable. Sharing a section transitively shares every file in it now and in the future (resolution happens at query time via `_ids_of_files_shared_with`).

### Access control
- Owners can access their own files (read + write).
- Super admins can access all files (read + write).
- Any user with a `FileShare` row where `shared_with_user_id = me` AND (`file_id = this` OR `section_id = this.section_id`) can **read** + **download** the file. They cannot move / rename / delete it (`_user_owns_file` is the gate; `_user_can_view_file` is the read gate).
- View-only users (`can_generate() == False`) still cannot access `/user/files` at all (403). They can still receive shared rows, but the page itself is gated on `can_generate()`.

### GeneratedFile status lifecycle
`pending` → `generating` → `completed` | `failed`

The My Files page polls every **5 seconds**, but only re-fetches sections that actually contain a `.status-generating` row — much lighter than the old full-page reload.

### Frontend conventions
- Sections list + files render lives in `templates/my_files.html`. Per-section state is held in a `sectionState` Map keyed by `section_id`.
- File drag uses `Sortable({group:'oqb-files'})` per `<tbody class="section-files-tbody" data-section-id="...">`. Cross-section drop fires `onAdd` → `/user/files/<id>/move`; same-section drag fires `onUpdate` → `/user/files/reorder`. Read-only (`data-readonly="1"`) rows are filter-blocked. The Shared-with-me virtual section sets `put:false, pull:false`.
- Section vertical reorder uses `Sortable({group:'oqb-sections'})` on `#sectionsContainer`, filtered against `.is-default, .is-shared` so those are pinned.
- **Drag uses `preventOnFilter: false`** on BOTH sortables — otherwise SortableJS would call `event.preventDefault()` on every mouse event inside filtered cards (Latest, Shared-with-me), killing native `<select>` dropdowns and dropdown-toggle buttons inside their headers. The `.section-drag-handle` is hidden via CSS on those cards so dragging is impossible anyway.
- **`onStart`/`onEnd` add/remove `body.oqb-dragging`** which applies global `user-select: none !important` for the duration of the drag, suppressing accidental text highlighting.
- **"Show all users" toggle**: the page header has a `#showAllToggle` checkbox (super-admin only). `reloadAll()` passes `show_all=1` to both `/user/sections` and every `/user/files/list` call. Foreign sections render a blue `@username` owner pill in their header (via `s.owner_username`); the Move-to dropdown then includes every visible section as a destination so admins can reorganise other users' files in place.
- **Search is server-side**. The top-bar input updates a module-level `currentSearch` and (debounced 250 ms) triggers `loadSection(id, 1)` for every loaded section with `q=<query>` appended. Section file-count badges automatically pick up the post-filter `total`; the empty-state message switches to `No files match "<query>"`. Highlighting of the match inside the rendered row is still client-side (`<mark class="oqb-search-hit">`).
- **Lazy PDF button** (red, beside the green Download). Driven by `pdf_supported` + `pdf_available` on each row dict. The `<a href>` link variant is used when the sibling PDF is already cached on disk; the `<button>` + `buildAndDownloadPdf()` fetch flow is used when it isn't — it hits `GET /generate/pdf/<id>`, shows a spinner for the duration of the (synchronous) Word COM conversion, then saves the streamed bytes via blob URL and reloads the section so the button flips to the link variant. Hidden entirely when `pdf_supported=false` (e.g. a legacy `.pdf` row). Deleting a row also removes any cached sibling PDF.
- Polling, bulk bar, and toast UX are all client-side; no HTMX involvement.
- **Header layout**: title row (with super-admin "Show all users" switch + Refresh on the right) sits above a separate `.card` toolbar containing the search input (left, `flex: 1 1 240px`) and **New section** button (right). The two-row split keeps the page from wrapping awkwardly at narrow widths.
